---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contributing — nSealr" description="Current public source, contribution workflow and private vulnerability reporting.">
  <section class="container page">
    <p class="eyebrow">// contributing</p>
    <h1 class="page__title">Work on the current public source.</h1>
    <p class="lead">nSealr is pre-release. The first milestone joins three device paths with the client, Bridge and TypeScript SDK needed to use them. Public-fixture evidence is useful development progress; it is not a production-security or complete interoperability claim.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">Where work lives</h2>
    <ul class="page__list">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr">nsealr</a>: shared Rust engine, ESP32-S3, Raspberry Pi and ESP32-P4 apps, Bridge/CLI/service/client/browser packages, TypeScript SDK and contracts. The sole public task graph owns accepted scope and evidence.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/website">website</a>: current public documentation and site.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/.github">.github</a>: shared contribution and security guidance.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/nSealr/hardware">hardware</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/board-sdk">board-sdk</a>: retained future board work, not a prerequisite for the initial device profiles.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The companion, raspberry and specs repositories retain migration history. Open current software issues and pull requests in nsealr. Smartcard research is retired; do not turn old research guides into current installation instructions.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">Development and review</h2>
    <p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">shared contribution workflow</a> and <a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">public development quickstart</a>. They use the consolidated public source and pinned Linux bootstrap, without a private lab checkout.</p>
    <p>Use focused checks during development, preserve significant failures and exact source/artifact identities, obtain distinct review and satisfy the repository's protected delivery gates. A requirement, independent expected result and relevant adverse case matter more than a phrase check or a coverage percentage. Hardware and installed-client claims need their own evidence.</p>
    <h2 class="page__h2">Disclosure</h2>
    <p>Use the <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/security/advisories/new">central private vulnerability report form</a> and <a href="https://github.com/nSealr/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md">shared security policy</a>. Do not publish sensitive details in an issue, pull request or log. No unverified private-message or email channel is assumed.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: var(--space-20); max-width: 880px; }
  .page__title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-strong);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  .page__h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-strong);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .lead { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .page__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 80ch;
    padding-left: 1em;
  }
  .page__why { font-size: var(--text-base); margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; }
</style>
